significant health risks. It is particularly concerning in patients with liver cirrhosis, as it increases the risk of hepatic encephalopathy, a serious complication of liver dysfunction. Additionally, muscle depletion is a critical issue in cancer patients, where it is often linked to cancer cachexia—a syndrome that leads to severe weight loss and muscle wasting. This condition adversely affects the prognosis of cancer patients, highlighting the importance of addressing muscle depletion in both liver disease and cancer care.", "HEPATIC ENCEPHALOPATHY:Hepatic encephalopathy is a decline in brain function that occurs as a result of severe liver disease. This condition leads to a buildup of toxins in the bloodstream, which can significantly impair cognitive function and overall neurological health.", "CIRRHOSIS:Cirrhosis is a chronic liver disease characterized by the replacement of healthy liver tissue with scar tissue, which leads to liver dysfunction and can progress to liver failure. It represents a late stage of scarring (fibrosis) of the liver, resulting from various liver diseases and conditions, including hepatitis and chronic alcoholism. Additionally, cirrhosis increases the risk of developing hepatocellular carcinoma, a type of liver cancer.", "MELD:MELD (Model for End-Stage Liver Disease) is a scoring system used to assess the severity of chronic liver disease and prioritize patients for liver transplantation.", "PROTEIN-CALORIE MALNUTRITION:Protein-calorie malnutrition is a condition that occurs when the body does not get enough protein and calories, which can be particularly detrimental in patients with liver cirrhosis.", "MONTANO-LOZA AJ:Montano-Loza AJ is a researcher and author known for his significant contributions to the field of liver transplantation and cirrhosis. He has published studies focusing on muscle wasting and its implications for liver transplantation outcomes. Additionally, Montano-Loza AJ has investigated the association between sarcopenia, a condition characterized by the loss of muscle mass, and mortality in patients suffering from cirrhosis. His work highlights the critical relationship between muscle health and patient prognosis in liver-related diseases.", "TANDON P:Tandon P is a researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the field of liver health. They have studied the prevalence of severe muscle depletion in patients on the liver transplant waitlist, highlighting the critical health challenges faced by these individuals. Additionally, Tandon P has contributed to a meta-analysis on nutritional supplementation in cirrhosis, further emphasizing their commitment to advancing knowledge and improving patient outcomes in liver disease.", "HARA N:Hara N is a researcher who has investigated the prognostic factors for overall survival in patients with cirrhosis.", "CARIAS S:Carias S is a researcher who has studied the association between nonalcoholic steatohepatitis and sarcopenic obesity in cirrhosis patients.", "PERIYALWAR P:Periyalwar P is a researcher who has explored the consequences of malnutrition in cirrhosis.", "MCULLOUGH AJ:McCullough AJ is a researcher who has studied protein-calorie malnutrition and its role in the etiology of cirrhosis."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}